.Dd November 21, 2026
.Dt RMXOS-INSTALL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm rmxos-install
.Nd write a whole fresh rmxOS disk from a full stream
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl -disk Ar disk
.Fl -catalog Ar DIR | URL
.Oo
.Fl -hostname Ar name
.Fl -user Ar name
.Fl -key Ar file
.Oc
.Op Fl -profile Ar disk|live|vm
.Op Fl -profile-file Ar file
.Op Fl -console Ar list
.Op Fl -owner Ar now|later
.Op Fl -pool Ar name
.Op Fl -altroot Ar dir
.Op Fl -swap Ar size
.Op Fl -zone Ar name
.Op Fl -erase
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
writes
.Ar disk
in the shape every
.Xr softwareupdate 8
update leaves, without asking anything, for UEFI machines:
.Bl -enum
.It
A GPT with a 260 MB FAT32 ESP, optional swap of
.Ar size ,
and one ZFS partition.
There is no BIOS boot partition.
.It
The pool
.Ar name
(default
.Cm Pool )
created under the alternate root
.Ar dir
(default
.Pa /mnt )
with
.Cm mountpoint=none ,
.Cm atime=off ,
.Cm compression=lz4
and no cache file.
.It
The catalog's full stream received by softwareupdate's engine onto
.Ar pool Ns /Update/ Ns Ar lineage ,
its snapshot cloned to
.Ar pool Ns /System/ Ns Ar snapshot ,
held as
.Cm rmxos-head
and set as the pool's
.Cm bootfs .
.It
Data:
.Ar pool Ns /Data
and its
.Cm private ,
.Cm Users
(case-insensitive),
.Cm Library
and
.Cm local ,
with
.Pa /private/etc
populated from the base's template by
.Pa /usr/libexec/rmxos-datasync .
.It
The machine's seeds on Data:
.Pa rc.conf
with DHCP on the default interface and
.Cm sshd_enable
enabled;
.Pa localtime
from
.Ar zone
(default
.Cm UTC ) ;
and the first
.Cm installed
line of the update history.
If all three owner options are supplied, the shared
.Xr rmxos-owner 8
writer also sets the hostname, adds the first user and home
.Pa /Users/ Ns Ar name ,
whose only login is the public key in
.Ar file ,
and who becomes root with
.Xr mdo 1
by a
.Va security.mac.do.rules
line in
.Pa sysctl.conf ;
and locks root's password.
With all three options omitted the template's users and empty root
password are retained, and no owner or mac_do rule is written.
Root then works only on the console: the base sshd configuration refuses
root logins and empty passwords.
A partial owner option set refuses before any write.
An owner can be added later with
.Xr rmxos-owner 8 ,
which takes the same three options, or at boot by
.Xr rmxos-owner-seed 8 .
.It
The environment's
.Pa /boot/loader.efi
at every ESP path an update refreshes
.Pq see Xr softwareupdate 8 :
.Pa EFI/BOOT/BOOTX64.EFI ,
which the firmware starts because no boot entry is made, and
.Pa efi/freebsd/loader.efi ;
and
.Pa efi/freebsd/loader.env
holding only the console lines for
.Ar list ,
a comma-separated list of loader consoles
.Pq Cm comconsole , efi , vidconsole , nullconsole , spinconsole .
No update rewrites
.Pa loader.env .
.El
.Pp
Everything is unmounted and the pool exported at the end; the machine's own
loader imports it.
.Pp
Before any write,
.Nm
refuses a disk that holds the running root, an imported pool, a mount or
swap, a disk that is not empty (it has a partition table, or its first or
last MiB is not zero) unless
.Fl -erase
is given, and a catalog without a full stream.
All providers in the disk's GEOM subtree count, including encryption,
NOP, mirror and label providers above its partitions.
A failed GEOM, partition-table, imported-pool, mount or swap lookup refuses
the install and reports that nothing was written.
With
.Fl -erase ,
an existing partition table is destroyed before erasing the disk's ends;
a failed table destruction stops the install.
A failure part-way names what was made, unmounts and exports the pool.
.Sh DATASET NAMES AND EARLY VALIDATION
Build snapshots use
.Cm Tag-
followed by seven lowercase hexadecimal commit digits.
Reserved pool names
.Cm mirror ,
.Cm raidz ,
.Cm draid ,
.Cm spare
and names beginning with those strings, and the exact name
.Cm log ,
are refused before any write; the match is case-sensitive.
A zero swap size is also refused before any write.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width RMXOS_SU_FIXTURE
.It Ev RMXOS_SU_FIXTURE
A host test directory: only an
.Xr md 4
disk backed by a file below it, an alternate root below it and a pool whose
name starts with
.Cm rmxsu
are accepted.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when the disk is written, 1 after a one-line refusal or failure, 2 for a
usage error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mdo 1 ,
.Xr mac_do 4 ,
.Xr rmxos-owner 8 ,
.Xr rmxos-owner-seed 8 ,
.Xr softwareupdate 8 ,
.Xr zpool 8
.Sh IMAGE PROFILES
The
.Fl profile Ar disk|live|vm
option selects an embedded plain key=value profile from
.Pa usr.sbin/rmxos-install/profiles
in the source tree; disk is the default.
.Fl profile-file Ar file
instead reads a local replacement in the same format, before any write.
Required scalar keys are pool, console, swap (none or a size), and owner
(now or later). Repeating rc and loader keys append configuration lines;
repeating data keys create empty files at absolute paths on Data.
Unknown keys, duplicate scalar keys, incomplete records, and unknown consoles
are refused. Command-line pool, console, swap and owner options override
profile values regardless of argument order. Supplying the complete owner
option set requests owner creation now; explicit owner=later conflicts with it.
An owner=now profile requires the complete owner option set.
.Pp
Disk and VM use Pool; live uses Install-rmxOS. All default to no swap and
owner provisioning later. Disk and live use comconsole,efi; VM uses comconsole.
VM enables growfs once and creates /private/var/db/firstboot on Data.
The console is optional when a profile supplies it. --swap none disables swap.
